ind this number such that rearranging its digits forms the difference \\(\\overline{a b c d} - \\overline{d c b a}\\).\n\n1. **Algebraic Representation**:\n   - Original number: \\(N = 1000a + 100b + 10c + d\\)\n   - Reversed number: \\(M = 1000d + 100c + 10b + a\\)\n   - Difference: \\(N - M = 999(a - d) + 90(b - c)\\)\n\n2. **Key Observations**:\n   - The difference \\(N - M\\) must be a permutation of the digits \\(a, b, c, d\\).\n   - The sum \\(a + b + c + d\\) must be divisible by 9 (since \\(N - M\\) is a multiple of 9).\n\n3. **Systematic Exploration**:\n   - We explored possible values for \\(a - d\\) (denoted as \\(k\\)) and \\(b - c\\) (denoted as \\(m\\)).\n   - For \\(k = 6\\) and \\(m = 2\\), we found:\n     - \\(a = 7\\), \\(d = 1\\), \\(b = 6\\), \\(c = 4\\)\n     - The original number \\(N = 7641\\)\n     - Reversed number \\(M = 1467\\)\n     - Difference \\(N - M = 7641 - 1467 = 6174\\), which is a permutation of the digits 7, 6, 4, 1.\n\n4. **Verification**:\n   - The digits of 6174 (6, 1, 7, 4) are a permutation of the original digits 7, 6, 4, 1.\n   - The sum \\(7 + 6 + 4 + 1 = 18\\) is divisible by 9.\n\nThus, the four-digit number is \\(\\boxed{7641}\\).", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. **Consider the subtraction:** \n   \n   \\[\n   \\overline{abcd} - \\overline{dcba}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identify the relationship between digits:** \n   \n   Since \\( a > b > c > d \\).\n\n3. **Rewrite subtraction in terms of digit places:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\begin{aligned}\n   \\text{Units place: } & e = 10 + d - a = 10 - (a - d) \\\\\n   \\text{Tens place: } & t = 10 + (c - 1) - b = 9 - (b - c) \\\\\n   \\text{Hundreds place: } & s = (b - 1) - c = (b - c) - 1 \\\\\n   \\text{Thousands place: } & k = a - d \\\\\n   \\end{aligned}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Evaluate constraints:**\n\n   \\[\n   k + e = 10 \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   s + t = 8\n   \\]\n\n5. **Check inequalities:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\begin{aligned}\n   t & = 9 - b + c \\\\\n     & \\geq 9 - (a - 1) + (d + 1) \\\\\n     &