ribed, the height of the frustum \\( h \\) is twice the radius of the sphere, \\( h = 2r \\).\n\n3. **Condition for Inscribed Sphere**:\n   - The distance from the center of the sphere to each lateral face must equal the radius \\( r \\).\n   - The center of the sphere is at \\( (0, 0, h/2) \\), and the distance from this center to a lateral face is \\( h/2 \\).\n\n4. **Deriving Relationships**:\n   - The necessary condition for the sphere to be tangent to the lateral face leads to the equation:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{(h/2)(A + B)}{\\sqrt{4h^2 + (B - A)^2}} = \\frac{h}{2}\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying this, we find:\n     \\[\n     A + B = 2a\n     \\]\n   - Additionally, the product of the side lengths \\( A \\) and \\( B \\) is related to the height:\n     \\[\n     AB = h^2\n     \\]\n\n5. **Lateral Surface Area Calculation**:\n   - The lateral surface area of a frustum is given by:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Lateral Surface Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (\\text{Perimeter of bottom base} + \\text{Perimeter of top base}) \\times \\text{Slant height}\n     \\]\n   - Substituting the perimeters of the square bases and the slant height \\( a \\):\n     \\[\n     \\text{Lateral Surface Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (4A + 4B) \\times a = 2(A + B) \\times a\n     \\]\n   - Using \\( A + B = 2a \\):\n     \\[\n     \\text{Lateral Surface Area} = 2 \\times 2a \\times a = 4a^2\n     \\]\n\nThus, the area of the lateral surface is \\(\\boxed{4a^2}\\).", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. **Assign Definitions:** Let \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) be the lengths of the sides of the bases of the pyramid. The height of the lateral face of the pyramid is given as \\( a \\).\n\n2. **Formulate the Area of One Lateral Face:** The lateral face of the pyramidal frustum forms a trapezoid with side lengths \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) (the bases of the trapezoid), and height \\( a \\) (the slant height of the trapezoid). Therefore, the area \\( A \\) of one lateral face is given by the formula for the area of